  "rationale": "Blocking the four collection steps that feed the target (dbReplica:collection, codeRepo:collection, shareMount:collection, vaultRead:collection) makes crownData:exfiltrate unreachable, so 4 blocks are enough. Three blocks cannot work. There are three attack paths that share no blockable step: (1) supplychain -> tokenCache -> monitoringHost -> codeRepo; (2) supplychain -> browserStore -> jumpHost -> shareMount; (3) phishing -> memoryDump -> fileServer -> vaultRead. Each of the three blocks must therefore sit on a different one of these paths, leaving none spare to stop dbReplica, which needs domainAdmin (backupHost AND ssoLogin). The only way to cut path 2 and also stop domainAdmin with one block is browserStore, which kills ssoLogin. But jumpHost is still reached from memoryDump, which forces blocking memoryDump. The third block must then stop both monitoringHost (fed by tokenCache) and backupHost (fed by configSecret), and no single step does both. Stopping domainAdmin through backupHost instead also leaves a surviving route in every 3-block combination. So the minimum is 4."
